[COMMENTS]
STATION,Flat V weir for low flow, with rated section for high flows. Designed by Flood Defence. GENERAL: Station is located 2km north west of the village of Milverton and was opened in 1991 as part of the flood warning system for Taunton. Designed by Flood Defence. Flat V weir for low flow, with rated section for high flows. STATION HYDROMETRY: Original rating was applied across period of record, based on theoretical flat V equation, altered because gaugings show lower than expected flows. Some scatter in gaugings and ratings are poor fit beyond 0.6m. Two peak flow ratings across period of record. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2022 (WINFAP Files v11). FLOW REGIME: Sewage treatment works upstream of site, and pig processing factory (having stream support borehole) 100m upstream of that. Discharge from sewage works is greater than abstraction.
CATCHMENT,Catchment predominantly comprising Permo-Triassic and Carboniferous mudstone, siltstone and sandstone. Land-use is rural. No major catchment changes.
Qmed Suitability,Although gauged to within 20% of QMED, rating is uncertain beyond 0.6m.
Pooling Suitability,Rating uncertain beyond 0.6m and does not fit well to available gaugings.
[END]
